  "body": "## What happens\n\n2D Contour with Side Auto on a picked rim of a BLIND bore resolves to Outside. The Outside ring stands in the part below the mouth. Before #1927 the operation cut only the top plane (in air) and posted with no warning. With the #1927 fix (PR on `issue/1927-contour-outside-hole-refusal`) the operation is refused by name (\"set Side to Inside\").\n\nFixture: `testdata/models/Milling-test.step`, the closed rim chain of radius 12.5 at Z 20. Test: `crates/app/tests/area_open.rs`, `a_containment_that_puts_the_tool_in_the_part_is_refused_by_name` (the last assert pins the refusal).\n\n## Cause\n\n`selection_geometry_impl` (`crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs`) resolves Auto by the fill ratio: the area of the ring that is part material, read from the part's XY silhouette. The floor of a blind bore fills the silhouette inside the rim. Thus the fill is near 1 and Auto selects Outside. A through hole has an empty silhouette inside the rim, so Auto selects Inside there.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Auto reads the material that the ring bounds at the ring's own level (or just below it), not the full XY silhouette.\n- Auto on a blind bore rim resolves to Inside and cuts the wall from inside.\n- The last assert of the test above changes to a clean Inside path.\n- Auto on a boss and on an outer wall still resolves to Outside.\n\n## Workaround\n\nSet Side to Inside.\n",
